  "rule": "Each 8-connected single-colour object keeps its shape and columns; if another object has the same cell count it slides up to touch the top edge, otherwise (unique cell count) it slides down to touch the bottom edge.",
  "scope": "Supported: grids 12..30 per side, any background colour 0..9, 3..7 objects of 2..12 cells grown as random 8-connected shapes in a 5x5 box (including diagonal-only contact), one or two shared-size groups (pairs or a triple) plus one or more unique-size distractors, optional repeated colours across objects, column overlap between a riser and a sinker, objects already at their edge as long as at least one moves. Not supported: objects touching each other in the input, multi-colour objects, shapes larger than 5x5, more than two shared-size groups, grids under 12 per side.",
  "constraints": [
    "No two objects are 8-adjacent in the input, so colour-aware and colour-blind connectivity agree on the decomposition.",
    "Output cells of distinct objects never overlap (checked at placement using the final destination rows).",
    "At least one object is not already at its destination edge (no identity examples).",
    "Background colour occupies more than half the grid, so it is the majority colour.",
    "The size multiset always contains at least one repeated size and at least one unique size; shared group sizes and unique sizes are mutually distinct values.",
    "Every shape is 8-connected with exact cell count and fits inside the grid at both its input and output positions."
  ],
  "known_limitations": [
    "Shapes are random growth blobs rather than the stylised rings/crosses/arrows of the originals; shapes within a shared-size group are not forced to differ.",
